nce.\n\n### 18. Claro. Para eso están los amigos.\n- **When:** 00:08:23\n- **Meaning:** Of course. That's what friends are for. *(subtitle line)*\n- **Before:** ¿Te echo una mano con la mudanza?\n- **After:** Te debo una, otra vez.\n- **Usage:** affirming that friends are there to help. Warm, supportive tone.\n\n### 19. Por cierto, ¿sigue lloviendo?\n- **When:** 00:08:59\n- **Meaning:** By the way, is it still raining? *(subtitle line)*\n- **Before:** ¡Salud!\n- **After:** A cántaros.\n- **Usage:** Checking if it’s still raining later. Small talk about weather.\n\n### 20. Eres un sol.\n- **When:** 00:09:16\n- **Meaning:** You're a sweetheart. *(subtitle line)*\n- **Before:** Ni hablar. Esta vez te acompaño a casa.\n- **After:** \n- **Usage:** Complimenting someone as a sweet person. Informal, friendly.\n\n## Self-quiz\n\n1. Say it: \"Good morning! What can I get you?\"\n2. Say it: \"A coffee with milk, please.\"\n3. Say it: \"Hey, it's going to rain. Do you have an umbrella?\"\n4. Say it: \"A very calm cat.\"\n5. Fill the gap: \"¡Lena! ¿Qué ___ por aquí?\" (Answer: haces)\n6. Fill the gap: \"El ___ y dos. Pasa cada diez minutos.\" (Answer: treinta)\n7. Fill the gap: \"If you don't ___ in three days, go to the doctor.\" (Answer: improve)\n8. What does it mean: \"Para llevar. Tengo un poco de prisa.\" a) I want it to stay. b) I'm in a hurry to take it away. c) I want it to go, I'm in a hurry. (Answer: c)\n9. What does it mean: \"Le recomiendo estas pastillas para la garganta.\" a) I suggest drinking water. b) I recommend these throat lozenges. c) I refuse the medication. (Answer: b)\n10. Which situation: You are offering to help a friend move furniture. Which phrase fits? (Answer: ¿Te echo una mano con la mudanza? (phrase 17, 00:08:15))\n\n## Answers\n\n1. ¡Buenos días! ¿Qué te pongo? (phrase 1, 00:00:04)\n2. Un café con leche, por favor. (phrase 2, 00:00:07)\n3. Oye, va a llover. ¿Tienes paraguas? (phrase 8, 00:01:16)\n4. Un gato muy tranquilo. (phrase 12, 00:04:45)\