d \"Yes with flashcards\". Then we created folder; asked to confirm folder creation (user approved). Then we checked file existence; none exists. So we can proceed to saving sheet.\n\nNow we need to produce the sheet text, flashcards text, then save both.\n\nThus we need to produce phrases. This will require reasoning over the subtitle content. We need to parse the Spanish subtitles (0-~136). They have 136 entries (but clipped at 136 in the reading). Actually Spanish file had entries up to ID 136 (which ends with \"Eres un sol.\").\n\nWe need to create a list of phrases. Use intermediate level selection: up to 20. Should pick phrases that are everyday useful, medium length, etc. At most 12 words per phrase, context lines up to 15 words.\n\nAlso avoid names and places, filler lines, etc. Also avoid repeating ones from earlier sheet (none). Include before and after context lines.\n\nWe'll need to generate usage notes and short. Also generate flashcards (tab-separated phrase, translation, title+timestamp). Must include only those with translation (by alignment, paired). Since we have user-language subtitles, we can pair translations directly: each phrase's translation is the English subtitle line for same timestamp (or appropriate aligned offset). Since they are aligned, we can match same timestamps exactly.\n\nThus we need to produce a mapping: Spanish phrase -> English translation.\n\n**Plan**:\n\n- Parse Spanish entries.\n\nLet's list Spanish subtitles with indices, timestamps, text:\n\nBased on the es.srt content we saw earlier (from earlier read). Let's extract them with full content.\n\nThe Spanish srt entries (reproduced from earlier reading) are:\n\n1. 00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,940\n   ¡Buenos días! ¿Qué te pongo?\n\n2. 00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,635\n   Un café con leche, por favor.\n\n3. 00:00:11,585 --> 00:00:14,690\n   ¿Para tomar aquí o para llevar?\n\n4. 00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:19,270\n   Para llevar. Tengo un poco de prisa.\n\n5. 00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:22,305\n   Claro. ¿Algo más?\n\n6. 00:00:23,255 --> 00:00:25,975\n   No, gracias. ¿Cuánto es?\n\n7. 00:00:27,175 --> 00:00:30,115\n   Son dos euros con cincuenta.\n\n8. 00:00:30,815 --> 00:00:33,590\n   ¿Puedo pagar con tarjeta?\n\n9. 00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,875\n   Sí, sin problema.\n\n10. 00:00:38,075 --> 00:00:40,960\n    ¡Lena! ¿Qué haces por aquí?\n\n11. 00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:44,325\n    ¡Marco! Qué casualidad.\n\n12. 00:00:45,275 --> 00:00:47,665\n    ¿Ya te has mudado?\n\n13. 00:00:48,865 --> 00:00:51,970\n    Todavía no. Sigo buscando piso.\n\n14. 00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:55,940\n    ¿En serio? ¿Y cómo va la búsqueda?\n\n15. 00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,720\n    Regular. Todo es carísimo.\n\n16. 00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,750\n    Te entiendo perfectamente.\n\n17. 00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:07,610\n    Hoy tengo una visita a las once.\n\n18. 00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,335\n    ¿Quieres que te acompañe?\n\n19. 00:01:12,535 --> 00:01:15,475\n    No hace falta, pero gracias.\n\n20. 00:01:16,175 --> 00:01:19,500\n    Oye, va a llover. ¿Tienes paraguas?\n\n21. 00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:23,225\n    No, se me olvidó en casa.\n\n22. 00:01:24,425 --> 00:01:26,980\n    Toma, llévate el mío.\n\n23. 00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,850\n    ¿Estás seguro?\n\n24. 00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,345\n    Segurísimo. Me lo devuelves esta noche.\n\n25. 00:01:35,545 --> 00:01:37,935\n    Vale. Te debo una.\n\n26. 00:01:38,635 --> 00:01:42,510\n    No te preocupes. ¿Cenamos juntos a las nueve?\n\n27. 00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,795\n    Me parece genial.\n\n28. 00:01:46,995 --> 00:01:49,660\n    Perfecto. ¡Hasta luego!\n\n29. 00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,860\n    Aquí tienes tu café.\n\n30. 00:01:53,810 --> 00:01:57,410\n    Muchas gracias. ¡Que tengas un buen día!\n\n31. 00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:08,440\n    Perdone, ¿me puede ayudar?\n\n32. 00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,310\n    Claro, dígame.\n\n33. 00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:15,255\n    Busco el tren para el centro.\n\n34. 00:02:16,455 --> 00:02:19,065\n    Sale del andén cuatro.\n\n35. 00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:22,705\n    ¿A qué hora sale el próximo?\n\n36. 00:02:23,655 --> 00:02:27,530\n    A las diez y cuarto, pero hoy va con retraso.\n\n37. 00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,725\n    ¿Con retraso? ¿Cuánto tiempo?\n\n38. 00:02:32,425 --> 00:02:35,640\n    Unos veinte minutos, más o menos.\n\n39. 00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:39,750\n    Vaya. Tengo una cita a las once.\n\n40. 00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:44,440\n    Entonces le conviene tomar el autobús.\n\n41. 00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,190\n    ¿Está lejos de aquí la parada?\n\n42. 00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:52,355\n    No, está a cinco minutos andando.\n\n43. 00:02:53,555 --> 00:02:57,755\n    Salga por la puerta principal y gire a la izquierda.\n\n44. 00:02:58,455 --> 00:03:01,560\n    ¿Y qué autobús tengo que coger?\n\n45. 00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:06,165\n    El treinta y dos. Pasa cada diez minutos.\n\n46. 00:03:07,365 --> 00:03:11,075\n    ¿Puede repetirlo, por favor? Más despacio.\n\n47. 00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:15,155\n    El treinta y dos, cada diez minutos.\n\n48. 00:03:16,105 --> 00:03:19,595\n    Perfecto. Muchas gracias por su ayuda.\n\n49. 00:03:20,795 --> 00:03:23,350\n    De nada. ¡Buen viaje!\n\n50. 00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:26,770\n    Señora Ortiz? Soy Lena.\n\n51. 00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:31,210\n    Lo siento, voy a llegar un poco tarde.\n\n52. 00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:35,845\n    No pasa nada. Te espero en el portal.\n\n53. 00:03:36,545 --> 00:03:39,320\n    Gracias por su paciencia.\n\n54. 00:03:47,270 --> 00:03:50,265\n    Pasa, pasa. Este es el salón.\n\n55. 00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:53,635\n    ¡Qué luminoso!\n\n56. 00:03:54,335 --> 00:03:58,100\n    Da al sur, así que tiene sol toda la tarde.\n\n57. 00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:01,990\n    ¿Cuántas habitaciones tiene?\n\n58. 00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:06,075\n    Dos habitaciones y un baño.\n\n59. 00:04:06,775 --> 00:04:09,330\n    ¿Puedo ver la cocina?\n\n60. 00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:13,660\n    Por supuesto. Está recién reformada.\n\n61. 00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:17,910\n    ¿Cuánto es el alquiler al mes?\n\n62. 00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:21,990\n    Ochocientos euros, gastos incluidos.\n\n63. 00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:25,660\n    ¿Incluye la calefacción?\n\n64. 00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:29,855\n    Sí, la calefacción y el agua.\n\n65. 00:04:30,555 --> 00:04:33,165\n    ¿Hay que pagar fianza?\n\n66. 00:04:34,115 --> 00:04:36,615\n    Dos meses de fianza.\n\n67. 00:04:37,815 --> 00:04:40,370\n    ¿Se admiten mascotas?\n\n68. 00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:44,065\n    Depende. ¿Qué mascota tienes?\n\n69. 00:04:45,015 --> 00:04:47,625\n    Un gato muy tranquilo.\n\n70. 00:04:48,825 --> 00:04:51,490\n    Un gato no es problema.\n\n71. 00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:55,075\n    ¿Cuándo estaría disponible?\n\n72. 00:04:56,025 --> 00:04:58,580\n    A partir del día uno.\n\n73. 00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:03,325\n    Hay otra persona interesada, la verdad.\n\n74. 00:05:04,025 --> 00:05:06,855\n    Entiendo. Déjeme pensarlo.\n\n75. 00:05:07,805 --> 00:05:10,800\n    Claro. ¿Me dices algo mañana?\n\n76. 00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,160\n    Sí, le escribo mañana sin falta.\n\n77. 00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:18,745\n    Muy bien. ¡Ay, cómo llueve!\n\n78. 00:05:19,695 --> 00:05:22,690\n    Menos mal que llevo paraguas.\n\n79. 00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:34,435\n    Buenas tardes. ¿En qué le puedo ayudar?\n\n80. 00:05:35,135 --> 00:05:37,910\n    No me encuentro muy bien.\n\n81. 00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:40,975\n    ¿Qué le pasa?\n\n82. 00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:45,830\n    Me duele la garganta y estoy muy cansada.\n\n83. 00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:48,700\n    ¿Desde cuándo?\n\n84. 00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:52,370\n    Desde ayer por la noche.\n\n85. 00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,740\n    ¿Tiene fiebre?\n\n86. 00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:59,710\n    Creo que no, pero no estoy segura.\n\n87. 00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:04,645\n    Le recomiendo estas pastillas para la garganta.\n\n88. 00:06:05,845 --> 00:06:08,730\n    Tome una cada cuatro horas.\n\n89. 00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:12,920\n    ¿Puedo tomarlas con el estómago vacío?\n\n90. 00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:16,535\n    Mejor después de comer.\n\n91. 00:06:17,735 --> 00:06:20,125\n    Y beba mucha agua.\n\n92. 00:06:20,825 --> 00:06:23,105\n    ¿Y si no mejoro?\n\n93. 00:06:24,055 --> 00:06:27,765\n    Si no mejora en tres días, vaya al médico.\n\n94. 00:06:28,965 --> 00:06:31,905\n    De acuerdo. ¿Cuánto le debo?\n\n95. 00:06:32,605 --> 00:06:35,215\n    Seis euros con veinte.\n\n96. 00:06:36,165 --> 00:06:38,170\n    Aquí tiene.\n\n97. 00:06:39,370 --> 00:06:41,540\n    Que se mejore.\n\n98. 00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,740\n    Gracias, muy amable.\n\n99. 00:06:52,690 --> 00:06:55,850\n    ¡Por fin! Pensaba que no venías.\n\n100. 00:06:57,050 --> 00:07:00,100\n    Perdona, llego tarde otra vez.\n\n101. 00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:04,015\n    No te preocupes. Acabo de llegar.\n\n102. 00:07:04,965 --> 00:07:08,620\n    Toma, tu paraguas. Me ha salvado la vida.\n\n103. 00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,265\n    ¿Qué tal la visita?\n\n104. 00:07:12,965 --> 00:07:15,960\n    Muy bien. El piso me encanta.\n\n105. 00:07:16,910 --> 00:07:19,025\n    ¿Y el precio?\n\n106. 00:07:20,225 --> 00:07:23,385\n    Un poco caro, pero vale la pena.\n\n107. 00:07:24,085 --> 00:07:26,475\n    ¿Vas a quedártelo?\n\n108. 00:07:27,425 --> 00:07:31,135\n    Creo que sí. Mañana le escribo a la dueña.\n\n109. 00:07:32,335 --> 00:07:35,550\n    ¡Enhorabuena! Hay que celebrarlo.\n\n110. 00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:38,585\n    ¿Qué van a tomar?\n\n111. 00:07:39,535 --> 00:07:42,035\n    ¿Qué nos recomienda?\n\n112. 00:07:43,235 --> 00:07:46,230\n    La paella está muy buena hoy.\n\n113. 00:07:46,930 --> 00:07:49,870\n    Pues dos paellas, por favor.\n\n114. 00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:53,870\n    Y una botella de agua sin gas.\n\n115. 00:07:55,070 --> 00:07:57,020\n    Enseguida.\n\n116. 00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:01,045\n    Oye, ¿estás bien? Tienes mala cara.\n\n117. 00:08:01,995 --> 00:08:05,265\n    Estoy un poco resfriada, nada más.\n\n118. 00:08:06,465 --> 00:08:09,955\n    Deberías descansar este fin de semana.\n\n119. 00:08:10,655 --> 00:08:14,530\n    Tienes razón. Pero tengo mil cosas que hacer.\n\n120. 00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,695\n    ¿Te echo una mano con la mudanza?\n\n121. 00:08:19,895 --> 00:08:22,890\n    ¿De verdad? Eso sería genial.\n\n122. 00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:26,805\n    Claro. Para eso están los amigos.\n\n123. 00:08:27,755 --> 00:08:30,365\n    Te debo una, otra vez.\n\n124. 00:08:31,565 --> 00:08:34,780\n    Me debes dos. Pero ¿quién cuenta?\n\n125. 00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,365\n    ¿Qué quieres decir con eso?\n\n126. 00:08:39,315 --> 00:08:42,530\n    Que me invites a la próxima cena.\n\n127. 00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:45,790\n    Trato hecho.\n\n128. 00:08:46,490 --> 00:08:49,430\n    Aquí tienen. ¡Que aproveche!\n\n129. 00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,715\n    ¡Qué buena pinta!\n\n130. 00:08:53,915 --> 00:08:56,305\n    Por el piso nuevo.\n\n131. 00:08:57,005 --> 00:08:58,790\n    ¡Salud!\n\n132. 00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,735\n    Por cierto, ¿sigue lloviendo?\n\n133. 00:09:03,935 --> 00:09:05,940\n    A cántaros.\n\n134. 00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:10,350\n    Entonces me vuelves a prestar el paraguas.\n\n135. 00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14:845\n    Ni hablar. Esta vez te acompaño a casa.\n\n136. 00:09:16,045 --> 00:09:18,105\n    Eres un sol.\n\nOkay.\n\nNow English subtitles, same number and close timestamps. Let's also note English lines for alignment.\n\nEnglish srt entries (we'll map them by index as they seem aligned one-to-one). Based on en.srt content we read earlier.\n\nEnglish entries:\n\n1. 00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,940\n   Good morning! What can I get you?\n\n2. 00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,635\n   A coffee with milk, please.\n\n3. 00:00:11,585 --> 00:00:14,690\n   For here or to go?\n\n4. 00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:19,270\n   To go. I'm in a bit of a hurry.\n\n5. 00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:22,305\n   Sure. Anything else?\n\n6. 00:00:23,255 --> 00:00:25,975\n   No, thanks. How much is it?\n\n7. 00:00:27,175 --> 00:00:30,115\n   That's two euros fifty.\n\n8. 00:00:30,815 --> 00:00:33,590\n   Can I pay by card?\n\n9. 00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:36,875\n   Yes, no problem.\n\n10. 00:00:38,075 --> 00:00:40,960\n    Lena! What are you doing here?\n\n11. 00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:44,325\n    Marco! What a coincidence.\n\n12. 00:00:45,275 --> 00:00:47,665\n    Have you moved in yet?\n\n13. 00:00:48,865 --> 00:00:51,970\n    Not yet. I'm still looking for a flat.\n\n14. 00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:55,940\n    Really? And how is the search going?\n\n15. 00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,720\n    So-so. Everything is really expensive.\n\n16. 00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,750\n    I know exactly what you mean.\n\n17. 00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:07,610\n    I have a viewing at eleven today.\n\n18. 00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,335\n    Do you want me to come with you?\n\n19. 00:01:12,535 --> 00:01:15,475\n    There's no need, but thanks.\n\n20. 00:01:16,175 --> 00:01:19,500\n    Hey, it's going to rain. Do you have an umbrella?\n\n21. 00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:23,225\n    No, I left it at home.\n\n22. 00:01:24,425 --> 00:01:26,980\n    Here, take mine.\n\n23. 00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,850\n    Are you sure?\n\n24. 00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,345\n    Absolutely. Give it back to me tonight.\n\n25. 00:01:35,545 --> 00:01:37,935\n    OK. I owe you one.\n\n26. 00:01:38,635 --> 00:01:42,510\n    Don't worry about it. Shall we have dinner at nine?\n\n27. 00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,795\n    That sounds great.\n\n28. 00:01:46,995 --> 00:01:49,660\n    Perfect. See you later!\n\n29. 00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,860\n    Here's your coffee.\n\n30. 00:01:53,810 --> 00:01:57,410\n    Thank you very much. Have a nice day!\n\n31. 00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:08,440\n    Excuse me, could you help me?\n\n32. 00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:11,310\n    Of course, go ahead.\n\n33. 00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:15,255\n    I'm looking for the train to the city centre.\n\n34. 00:02:16,455 --> 00:02:19,065\n    It leaves from platform four.\n\n35. 00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:22,705\n    What time does the next one leave?\n\n36. 00:02:23,655 --> 00:02:27,530\n    At quarter past ten, but it's running late today.\n\n37. 00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,725\n    Late? How long?\n\n38. 00:02:32,425 --> 00:02:35,640\n    About twenty minutes, more or less.\n\n39. 00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:39,750\n    Oh no. I have an appointment at eleven.\n\n40. 00:02:40,950 --> 00:02:44,440\n    Then you'd better take the bus.\n\n41. 00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,190\n    Is the stop far from here?\n\n42. 00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:52,355\n    No, it's a five-minute walk.\n\n43. 00:02:53,555 --> 00:02:57,755\n    Go out the main door and turn left.\n\n44. 00:02:58,455 --> 00:03:01,560\n    And which bus do I need to take?\n\n45. 00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:06,165\n    The thirty-two. It comes every ten minutes.\n\n46. 00:03:07,365 --> 00:03:11,075\n    Could you repeat that, please? More slowly.\n\n47. 00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:15,155\n    The thirty-two, every ten minutes.\n\n48. 00:03:16,105 --> 00:03:19,595\n    Perfect. Thank you very much for your help.\n\n49. 00:03:20,795 --> 00:03:23,350\n    You're welcome. Have a good trip!\n\n50. 00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:26,770\n    Mrs Ortiz? It's Lena.\n\n51. 00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:31,210\n    I'm sorry, I'm going to be a bit late.\n\n52. 00:03:32,410 --> 00:03:35,845\n    That's fine. I'll wait for you at the entrance.\n\n53. 00:03:36,545 --> 00:03:39,320\n    Thank you for your patience.\n\n54. 00:03:47,270 --> 00:03:50,265\n    Come in, come in. This is the living room.\n\n55. 00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:53,635\n    It's so bright!\n\n56. 00:03:54,335 --> 00:03:58,100\n    It faces south, so it gets sun all afternoon.\n\n57. 00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:01,990\n    How many bedrooms does it have?\n\n58. 00:04:03,190 --> 00:04:06,075\n    Two bedrooms and a bathroom.\n\n59. 00:04:06,775 --> 00:04:09,330\n    Can I see the kitchen?\n\n60. 00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:13,660\n    Of course. It has just been renovated.\n\n61. 00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:17,910\n    How much is the rent per month?\n\n62. 00:04:18,610 --> 00:04:21,990\n    Eight hundred euros, bills included.\n\n63. 00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:25,660\n    Does that include heating?\n\n64. 00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:29,855\n    Yes, the heating and the water.\n\n65. 00:04:30,555 --> 00:04:33,165\n    Is there a deposit?\n\n66. 00:04:34,115 --> 00:04:36,615\n    Two months' deposit.\n\n67. 00:04:37,815 --> 00:04:40,370\n    Are pets allowed?\n\n68. 00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:44,065\n    It depends. What pet do you have?\n\n69. 00:04:45,015 --> 00:04:47,625\n    A very calm cat.\n\n70. 00:04:48,825 --> 00:04:51,490\n    A cat is no problem.\n\n71. 00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:55,075\n    When would it be available?\n\n72. 00:04:56,025 --> 00:04:58,580\n    From the first of the month.\n\n73. 00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:03,325\n    There's someone else interested, to be honest.\n\n74. 00:05:04,025 --> 00:05:06,855\n    I understand. Let me think about it.\n\n75. 00:05:07,805 --> 00:05:10,800\n    Of course. Will you let me know tomorrow?\n\n76. 00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,160\n    Yes, I'll write to you tomorrow without fail.\n\n77. 00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:18,745\n    Very good. Oh, look how it's raining!\n\n78. 00:05:19,695 --> 00:05:22,690\n    Good thing I have an umbrella.\n\n79. 00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:34,435\n    Good afternoon. How can I help you?\n\n80. 00:05:35,135 --> 00:05:37,910\n    I'm not feeling very well.\n\n81. 00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:40,975\n    What's wrong?\n\n82. 00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:45,830\n    My throat hurts and I'm very tired.\n\n83. 00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:48,700\n    Since when?\n\n84. 00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:52,370\n    Since last night.\n\n85. 00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,740\n    Do you have a fever?\n\n86. 00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:59,710\n    I don't think so, but I'm not sure.\n\n87. 00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:04,645\n    I recommend these throat lozenges.\n\n88. 00:06:05,845 --> 00:06:08,730\n    Take one every four hours.\n\n89. 00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:12,920\n    Can I take them on an empty stomach?\n\n90. 00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:16,535\n    Better after eating.\n\n91. 00:06:17,735 --> 00:06:20,125\n    And drink plenty of water.\n\n92. 00:06:20,825 --> 00:06:23,105\n    And if I don't get better?\n\n93. 00:06:24,055 --> 00:06:27,765\n    If you don't improve in three days, go to the doctor.\n\n94. 00:06:28,965 --> 00:06:31,905\n    All right. How much do I owe you?\n\n95. 00:06:32,605 --> 00:06:35,215\n    Six euros twenty.\n\n96. 00:06:36,165 --> 00:06:38,170\n    Here you are.\n\n97. 00:06:39,370 --> 00:06:41,540\n    Get well soon.\n\n98. 00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,740\n    Thank you, that's very kind.\n\n99. 00:06:52,690 --> 00:06:55,850\n    Finally! I thought you weren't coming.\n\n100. 00:06:57,050 --> 00:07:00,100\n    Sorry, I'm late again.\n\n101. 00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:04,015\n    Don't worry. I've just arrived.\n\n102. 00:07:04,965 --> 00:07:08,620\n    Here's your umbrella. It saved my life.\n\n103. 00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,265\n    How did the viewing go?\n\n104. 00:07:12,965 --> 00:07:15,960\n    Very well. I love the flat.\n\n105. 00:07:16,910 --> 00:07:19,025\n    And the price?\n\n106. 00:07:20,225 --> 00:07:23,385\n    A bit expensive, but it's worth it.\n\n107. 00:07:24,085 --> 00:07:26,475\n    Are you going to take it?\n\n108. 00:07:27,425 --> 00:07:31:135\n    I think so. I'll write to the owner tomorrow.\n\n(there's a minor formatting error for 108's timestamp: \"00:07:27,425 --> 00:07:31:135\". Assume correct end 00:07:31,135.)\n\n109. 00:07:32,335 --> 00:07:35,550\n    Congratulations! We have to celebrate.\n\n110. 00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:38,585\n    What will you have?\n\n111. 00:07:39,535 --> 00:07:42,035\n    What do you recommend?\n\n112. 00:07:43,235 --> 00:07:46,230\n    The paella is very good today.\n\n113. 00:07:46,930 --> 00:07:49,870\n    Then two paellas, please.\n\n114. 00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:53,870\n    And a bottle of still water.\n\n115. 00:07:55,070 --> 00:07:57,020\n    Right away.\n\n116. 00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:01,045\n    Hey, are you OK? You don't look well.\n\n117. 00:08:01,995 --> 00:08:05,265\n    I've got a bit of a cold, that's all.\n\n118. 00:08:06,465 --> 00:08:09,955\n    You should rest this weekend.\n\n119. 00:08:10,655 --> 00:08:14,530\n    You're right. But I have a thousand things to do.\n\n120. 00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,695\n    Shall I give you a hand with the move?\n\n121. 00:08:19,895 --> 00:08:22,890\n    Really? That would be great.\n\n122. 00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:26,805\n    Of course. That's what friends are for.\n\n123. 00:08:27,755 --> 00:08:30,365\n    I owe you one, again.\n\n124. 00:08:31,565 --> 00:08:34,780\n    You owe me two. But who's counting?\n\n125. 00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,365\n    What do you mean by that?\n\n126. 00:08:39,315 --> 00:08:42,530\n    That you buy me the next dinner.\n\n127. 00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:45,790\n    It's a deal.\n\n128. 00:08:46,490 --> 00:08:49,430\n    Here you are. Enjoy your meal!\n\n129. 00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,715\n    That looks delicious!\n\n130. 00:08:53,915 --> 00:08:56,305\n    To the new flat.\n\n131. 00:08:57,005 --> 00:08:58,790\n    Cheers!\n\n132. 00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,735\n    By the way, is it still raining?\n\n133. 00:09:03,935 --> 00:09:05,940\n    It's pouring.\n\n134. 00:09:06,640 --> 00:09:10,350\n    Then you'll lend me the umbrella again.\n\n135. 00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,845\n    No way. This time I'll walk you home.\n\n136. 00:09:16,045 --> 00:09:18,105\n    You're a sweetheart.\n\nNow need to pick 20 phrases (or less if not enough). Likely there are many candidates.\n\nFrom the Spanish cues for intermediate level: We need everyday useful phrases, up to 12 words. Many of the cues fit.\n\nWe also need to include context lines: before and after lines (previous and next cue texts). Need to capture those.\n\nNeed to avoid names or places only: we have names (Lena, Marco, etc.) but those appear within phrases. The rule says \"Names and places: a cue that is only a name or a place is removed. In a phrase with a vocative name, remove the name and keep the rest.\" So we need to handle vocative names: Example: \"¡Lena! ¿Qué haces por aquí?\" Contains name \"Lena!\" as vocative, we should remove name and keep rest? Actually we could drop the name, keep \"¿Qué haces por aquí?\" but maybe the phrase \"¿Qué haces por aquí?\" is useful. In Spanish, \"What are you doing here?\" Good phrase. So we can include phrase \"¿Qué haces por aquí?\" If we remove \"¡Lena!\", the timestamp would be same; but we need to present phrase as it appears? The rule says \"Keep the phrase exactly as in the cue, except when we remove names/places? It says \"Remove name and keep the rest\"? Actually 2. Remove lines that are not worth learning: \"Names and places: a cue that is only a name or a place (\"¡Anna!\", \"Paris.\") In a phrase with a vocative name (\"Nice to meet you, Mr. Grant\"), remove the name and keep the useful part.\" So we should modify the phrase to remove \"¡Lena!\" leaving \"¿Qué haces por aquí?\" That aligns with the sheet \"phrase\" column. The timestamp remains same.\n\nMake usage note accordingly.\n\nWe also have many everyday useful phrases: ordering, asking for help, directions, asking for price, making appointments, habits.\n\nWe must avoid filler-only cues, sound descriptions etc.\n\nAlso avoid songs etc.\n\nAll cues listed are typical dialogue — many are relevant. Need to choose about 20. We must distribute across five equal parts (by time). Let's compute total time range: first cue starts at 00:00:04, last cue at 00:09:16 (full). We'll approximate equal parts: 0-~00:02:00, 00:02:00-04:00, 04:00-06:00, 06:00-08:00, 08:00-09:16.\n\nBut we can approximate. We'll pick about 4 from each fifth to get 20.\n\nSimplify: We'll pick first five parts:\n\n**Part 1 (0:00:04 to ~2:00)** includes cues 1-30 approx. We'll choose 4 phrases:\n\n- 1: ¡Buenos días! ¿Qué te pongo? => \"Good morning! What can I get you?\" (Useful greeting