a hand with the move?\"\n- Choose four.\n\n**Part 5 (8:00-9:16) includes cues 121-136 approx (08:19 to 09:18). Choose 4:\n\n- 124: Me debes dos. Pero ¿quién cuenta? => \"You owe me two. But who's counting?\"\n- 128: Aquí tienen. ¡Que aproveche! => \"Here you are. Enjoy your meal!\"\n- 132: Por cierto, ¿sigue lloviendo? => \"By the way, is it still raining?\"\n- 135: Ni hablar. Esta vez te acompaño a casa. => \"No way. This time I'll walk you home.\"\n- Also maybe 136: Eres un sol. => \"You're a sweetheart.\"\n- Choose four.\n\nThat yields 20 phrases.\n\nNow we need to generate \"before\" and \"after\" context lines for each selected phrase. Should be preceding and following cue texts (in Spanish) as they appear. Note that for first phrase, before is none? We can leave before as maybe \"—\". But spec says \"line spoken before\". For first cue, before line missing, but we can use empty or indicate none. Usually they still include line before; if none, can be blank.\n\nWe need to ensure context lines are at most 15 words each. All lines are short (<15). Good.\n\nNow each phrase must have usage note: short, up to 25 words in English (user language), describing situation, register, grammar note.\n\nWe'll need to produce translation line: hold the English translation line, which is from corresponding English subtitle.\n\nNow we need to also produce flashcards: each line: phrase, translation, title + timestamp (title \"Umbrella Weather\" and timestamp like 00:00:04). Format: tab-separated.\n\nNow finalize sheet with header as per format reference: Title, EP_TAG empty (movie). File name: `Umbrella Weather - Spanish intermediate - 2026-11-09.md`. Flashcards name: `Umbrella Weather - Spanish intermediate - 2026-11-09 - flashcards.txt`.\n\nWe need to embed sections: metadata table, phrases block, self-quiz etc.\n\nWe must generate the self-quiz: 10 questions (4 Say it, 3 Fill gap, 2 What does it mean, 1 Which situation). According to spec, we need to include review if earlier 